.TH "cbor::error_category" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
cbor::error_category \- The \fRstd::error_category\fP of \fBcbor::error\fP\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/error\&.hpp>\fP
.SS "Public Member Functions"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "char const * \fBname\fP () const noexcept override"
.br
.RI "Gives the name of the category\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "std::string \fBmessage\fP (int const condition) const override"
.br
.RI "Gives the text of an error\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "std::error_condition \fBdefault_error_condition\fP (int const condition) const noexcept override"
.br
.RI "Gives the condition that an error compares equal to\&. "
.in -1c
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
The \fRstd::error_category\fP of \fBcbor::error\fP\&. 

A program reaches it through \fBcbor::category()\fP\&. \fR\fBname()\fP\fP gives \fR"cbor"\fP\&. \fR\fBmessage\fP\fP gives the text of the error, for example \fR"key not found"\fP, and \fR"unknown cbor \fBerror\fP"\fP for a value that is no \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP\&.

.PP
\fR\fBdefault_error_condition\fP\fP maps four errors to a \fRstd::errc\fP: \fRno_buffer_space\fP, \fRvalue_too_large\fP, \fRnot_enough_memory\fP and \fRio_error\fP, each to the \fRstd::errc\fP of the same name\&. Every other error maps to a condition of this category\&. So only these four compare equal to a \fRstd::errc\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
cbor::category()\&.name()                             → char const *
cbor::category()\&.message(condition)                 → std::string
cbor::category()\&.default_error_condition(condition) → std::error_condition
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
.nf
message: {}
call: std::error_code const e{cbor::error::no_buffer_space}
result: std::error_code cbor:21
call: e\&.default_error_condition()\&.category()\&.name()
result: "generic"
call: std::error_code const t{cbor::error::too_little_data}
result: std::error_code cbor:1
call: t\&.default_error_condition()\&.category()\&.name()
result: "cbor"
call: cbor::category()\&.message(13)
result: "key not found"
call: cbor::category()\&.message(0)
result: "unknown cbor error"

.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
    bool const space = std::error_code{cbor::error::no_buffer_space} == std::errc::no_buffer_space;  // true
    bool const other = std::error_code{cbor::error::too_little_data} == std::errc::no_message;       // false
    std::string const unknown = cbor::category()\&.message(0);                                         // "unknown cbor error"
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBcbor::category()\fP 

.PP
\fBstd::is_error_code_enum<cbor::error>\fP 
.RE
.PP

